  "title": "Expedition 70 Progress 87 Cargo Ship Docks to International Space Station - Feb. 17, 2024 ",
  "description": "The uncrewed Roscosmos ISS Progress 87 cargo spacecraft docked to the Zvezda service module Feb. 17 after launching to the International Space Station from the Baikonur Cosmodrome in Kazakhstan Feb. 14 on a Soyuz booster rocket. Progress is filled with about three tons of supplies and cargo and will remain docked to the space station for approximately six months.   Join NASA as we go forward to the Moon and on to Mars -- discover the latest on Earth, the Solar System and beyond with a weekly update in your inbox.  Subscribe at: https://www.nasa.gov/subscribe",
